    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class in the suite, and both of its cases (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW`, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation as a read-only computed field on the owner response, following the existing pattern for derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`, etc.).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (documenting the fixed table and the `UNKNOWN` default).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/LocalityResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 A small single-responsibility utility holding the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `localityOf(city)` method returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. Modeled on the existing `EntityUtils` static-utility style, so the table lives in one dedicated place rather than being embedded in the mapper.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired the derivation via `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(formatLocality(owner))\")` plus a `formatLocality` default method that delegates to `LocalityResolver.localityOf(owner.getCity())` \u2014 consistent with how the other derived fields are computed in this mapper.\n\nThe city-to-region lookup lives in its own reusable unit, the mapper just wires stored state to the derived DTO field, and no existing class absorbed unrelated logic.",
